<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Main Idea - How to answer</h1>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>How to answer</h2>
    <p>The main idea is the most important point.</p>
    <p>The other sentences give details, examples or explanations.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-green">
    <h2>Clues</h2>
    <p>Ask: “What is this mostly about?”</p>
    <p>Use this frame: “The main idea is [idea] because all the sentences support it.”</p>
    <p>One-sentence rule: can you explain the whole paragraph in one sentence?</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-pink">
    <h2>Two tests</h2>
    <p><strong>Headline test.</strong> Imagine the paragraph is a news story. What headline would fit?</p>
    <p><strong>Elimination.</strong> In a multiple-choice question, remove options that are too narrow (one detail only) or too broad (the whole text, not this paragraph).</p>
  </section>
</div>
